# Virtual environment
.venv/

# Raw candle cache — NEVER committed (charter §10, build prompt §2 invariant 9).
# Default cache lives outside the repo (see engine/data.py); this guards any
# override that points inside it.
data_cache/

# Local replay journals/state — journals belong on the orphan `data` branch
# only. Rooted patterns: the committed parity/dry-run journal COPIES under
# research_outputs/ must not be swallowed.
/journal/
/state/

# Session packet zips — ferried by the operator, not committed.
research_outputs/packets/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# --- charter §10 hygiene: journals & derived data live on orphan `data` branch only ---
research_outputs/tc1/**
research_outputs/tc4/**
research_outputs/tc5/**
research_outputs/s1/**
research_outputs/s2/**
research_outputs/s3/**
research_outputs/v3_anchor/**
research_outputs/census/**
research_outputs/census_run2/**
research_outputs/tierc2/**
research_outputs/tierc2_run2/**
research_outputs/tierc3/**
research_outputs/tierc3_run2/**
# committed manifests are the intended surface; keep them tracked
!research_outputs/**/build_manifest.json
!research_outputs/**/manifest.json

# operator-ferried session packets (transport bundles, never the source of record)
*.zip
research_outputs/packets/**

# Re-include the analysis products & provenance already in the index. The two
# manifest negations above under-cover: these 19 files are the source of record
# for TC/S/V3 phases, not journal payloads. Nested dir re-included first so git
# will descend into it (a negation cannot rescue a file under an excluded dir).
!research_outputs/s1/resampled/
!research_outputs/census/refetch_log.json
!research_outputs/census/retrieval_meta.json
!research_outputs/s1/resampled/resample_report.json
!research_outputs/s1/run_log.txt
!research_outputs/s2/run_log.txt
!research_outputs/tc1/run_log.txt
!research_outputs/tc1/run_log2.txt
!research_outputs/tc4/expectation_table.json
!research_outputs/tc4/run_log.txt
!research_outputs/tc5/run_log.txt
!research_outputs/v3_anchor/CELL_CARDS.md
!research_outputs/v3_anchor/ENGINE_LOGIC_EXTRACT.md
!research_outputs/v3_anchor/ROLLUPS_AND_HYPOTHESES.md
!research_outputs/v3_anchor/cards.json
!research_outputs/v3_anchor/determinism.json
!research_outputs/v3_anchor/hypotheses.json
!research_outputs/v3_anchor/pass1_results.json
!research_outputs/v3_anchor/pass2_results.json
!research_outputs/v3_anchor/rollups.json

!research_outputs/s3/run_log.txt
!research_outputs/s3/analyze_log.txt
!research_outputs/s3/analyze_log2.txt

# CENSUS-1b: large analysis substrate stays out (census large-substrate
# precedent); the manifest, determinism record and run log are the surface.
research_outputs/census1b/**
research_outputs/census1b_run2/**
/census1b_termini_enriched.jsonl
!research_outputs/census1b/build_manifest.json
!research_outputs/census1b/determinism.json
!research_outputs/census1b/analyze_log2.txt

# Reviewer hand-off staging — local-only, never committed.
_reviewer_box/

# Daily Brief archive — ops artifacts, untracked by design (A1.5); ignored so `git clean -fd` cannot remove them
research_outputs/brief/
tests/brief_fixture/out/

# Daily routine reports aged out of the exchange rolling window (2026-08-02).
# Same class as the brief archive above and ignored for the same reason: these
# are ops artifacts moved OUT of exchange/ precisely because they no longer need
# to be published or box-synced. They stay on disk and in the weekly workflow
# backup; keeping them tracked would defeat the move.
research_outputs/_daily_archive/

# --- BRIEF-2 panel (Amendment 2 §8.2) ---
# Captures and daily partitions are TRACKED: they are the record, and write-once
# partitions keep git growth linear rather than compounding.
# The consolidated view is a regenerable convenience over those partitions and is
# NOT a record, so it stays out of git.
briefs/panel/consolidated_*.parquet

# restored phase journals - staging only, never committed (ATHENA 2026-08-04)
research_outputs/_unarchived/**

# MC-1 / APOLLO ops substrate — display-only fetched klines, per-bar series,
# registry series and bulk tables. Same class as the SEQ8 bulk below: ops data,
# regenerable, and large enough to break a push. The build document carries the
# path+size+sha256 pointers, which are the intended surface.
research_outputs/mc1/**

# SEQ8 / DIONYSUS bulk outputs — untrackable (files exceed GitHub's 100 MB limit) and the only lane output missing from this list; a wildcard `git add -A` swept 3,567 MB of them into a commit on 2026-08-05 and GitHub rejected the whole branch push
research_outputs/seq8/**
research_outputs/seq8_run2/**

# CENSUS-2A / MC-2 substrate — same class as the SEQ8 and MC-1 bulk above.
# Listed BEFORE the directory can exist: CENSUS-2A bulk is born on D: per I2, so
# a C: path here is already a residency violation — but the 2026-08-05 incident
# was untracked-but-unignored bulk, and the rule that would have prevented it
# costs two lines. The build document's path+size+sha256 pointers are the
# intended surface.
research_outputs/census2a/**
research_outputs/mc2/**

# CENSUS-2B substrate — same class again, and the one member of the family that
# was MISSING from this list. Found 2026-08-15 during the M2 restore: census2a,
# seq8_run2, mc1 and mc2 were all covered, census2b was not, and the LaCie holds
# 2.1 GB / 261 files of it. Restoring under v2 (substrate is now permanently
# local) would have put untracked-but-unignored bulk back in the tree — the
# precise 2026-08-05 condition the two blocks above were written to prevent.
# Listed BEFORE the restore, not after.
research_outputs/census2b/**

# --- OPERATOR RULING 2026-08-15 (queue 005 M3): the census2a/2b MANIFESTS are
# TRACKED, following the census1b precedent above rather than the census2a one.
#
# The bulk stays ignored -- that is unchanged and is what keeps a push from
# being rejected.  What changes is that the manifest, which is the *description*
# of the bulk (names + sizes + sha256), becomes a committed surface, so a clone
# that has never seen the substrate can still say what it should contain and
# what it should hash to.  That is the same argument that keeps the _archive
# sidecars tracked.
#
# The nested mc2/ directory is re-included FIRST: a negation cannot rescue a
# file underneath a directory git was told not to descend into (the same trap
# recorded at the s1/resampled/ block above).
!research_outputs/census2a/mc2/
!research_outputs/census2a/*manifest*.json
!research_outputs/census2a/mc2/*manifest*.json
!research_outputs/census2b/*manifest*.json

# Spotlight suppression marker (M3, 2026-08-15).  An ops artifact, not a repo
# file.  EFFICACY IS NOT PROVEN for a subdirectory -- .metadata_never_index is
# documented for volume roots, and `mdutil -i off` refuses a subdirectory
# ("invalid operation"), so the authoritative exclusion is the Spotlight Privacy
# list, which needs the GUI or root.  Kept because it is free, reversible and
# the only lever available without sudo; see the M3 report's HALT-SOFT item.
.metadata_never_index

# Operator backup vault — 2.9 GB of estate/workflow zips plus their .sha256
# sidecars. The zips were already covered by the `*.zip` rule above; the
# sidecars were not, which is the only reason this directory showed as
# untracked. Same class as the packet zips: operator-ferried, never the source
# of record.
naiad-backups/

# Google Drive Desktop upload staging (FOUND 2026-08-15, queue 005 M4 -- NOT
# looked for; `git add -A` aborted on it with
# `fatal: unable to stat '.tmp.driveupload/1915'` because Drive moved the file
# out from under the scan).
#
# 7.8 GB across 952 entries when first measured at 12:59, down to 2.7 GB across
# 6 by 13:4x -- it drains as Drive uploads, which is WHY git aborted: git stat'd
# an entry that Drive removed mid-scan. Sitting in the REPO ROOT, untracked and
# -- until this line -- UNIGNORED. That is precisely the 2026-08-05 condition described
# three blocks up: untracked-but-unignored bulk that a wildcard `git add -A`
# will sweep into a commit and that GitHub will then reject. The file sizes
# match the phase archives (e.g. 242,926,299 B = tc1_2026-07-27.zip), so this is
# Drive staging the _archive tree for upload.
#
# THIS LINE ONLY STOPS GIT FROM SEEING IT. It does not address the real finding,
# which is reported to the operator rather than acted on: **Google Drive is
# syncing ~/Naiad.** DATA RESIDENCY v2 says everything Naiad reads is LOCAL and
# the LaCie is backup-only; an active cloud sync of the working tree is a
# residency condition nobody recorded. The v2 identity gate greps for OneDrive,
# com~apple~CloudDocs and Mobile Documents -- it does NOT detect Google Drive
# Desktop, so the gate passes cleanly on a cloud-synced repo.
#
# NOTHING WAS DELETED. This directory is Drive's working state, not Naiad's.
.tmp.driveupload/

# launchd agent logs (QUEUE 005 M4, 2026-08-15).  StandardOutPath /
# StandardErrorPath for com.naiad.{daily,estate,workflow}.  Ops artifacts in the
# same class as the brief archive and the daily archive above: they are the
# machine's record of a scheduled run, they grow without bound, and they are not
# the source of record -- the build documents and the .sha256 sidecars are.
# Added BEFORE the agents were loaded, so the first scheduled run cannot put an
# untracked-but-unignored log into the tree.
logs/

# macOS Finder metadata.
.DS_Store

# Per-machine Claude Code harness settings. Scoped to the one file: the shared
# .claude/commands/ skills ARE tracked and must stay that way.
.claude/settings.local.json
